  "description": "SEJPED crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: 4(C16 H36 N1 1+),C88 H104 Eu4 O36 S8 4-,6(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1C (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1E (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1F (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.766-3.823 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.46-106.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (nBu4N)4[Eu4(L)2(OH)4(AcO)4]·6DMF (C170H290Eu4N10O42S8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
